subtasks.description:
Create tests/sdk-schema.test.ts (vitest, imports from ../src/engine/sdk-schema.js). For EVERY exported named schema (SystemInitSchema, SystemStatusSchema, StreamEventSchema, AssistantMessageSchema, ToolProgressSchema, UserMessageSchema, ResultEnvelopeSchema, ResultDetailSchema, RateLimitEventSchema) assert three things:
1. a well-formed fixture parses ok;
2. the same fixture with extra unknown top-level AND nested fields (e.g. `future_field: {...}`) still parses ok with NO issues — tolerance of unknown additional fields;
3. a malformed fixture with a required field deleted or retyped fails, and the returned issues[0].path is exactly the expected dotted/bracketed path (e.g. `session_id`, `message.content[0].type`, `event.type`, `tool_use_id`, `subtype`).
Also test formatPath/parseWith directly: a nested array index renders as `a.b[1].c`, and parseWith never throws on null/undefined/a primitive/a circular object. Drive the fixtures from SDK_SHAPES.md so the happy-path shapes are realistic.
